hi my name's Scott Williamson and I'm  the CEO of the mega center here in  reading I'm Julie soulfood one of the  family support workers here at mega  center just wanted to say thank you  we're here in volunteers week and it's a  great opportunity to celebrate all the  fantastic work that volunteers do across  our community I've been struck over the  last few months about the amazing work  that volunteers have done as they've  stepped forward to support the  vulnerable the isolated the scared  residents in our community as we've had  the corona virus pandemic it's been  amazing to see the work that's been done  we've had such great feedback from  residents who have really valued the  work that's been done but also from the  volunteers themselves who have felt  really wonderful to be part of a bigger  team somebody said that sometimes it's  just a friendly voice at the end of the  phone that could make all the difference  being a volunteer can help you  individually as well it can alleviate  stress anger anxiety give you some  fantastic skills to take forward to put  on your CV if you're looking for paid  work so we just want to say again just  thank you so so much because by your  volunteering over these last few months  you have made a big big difference in  our community and when you just want to  say thank you but we want to say  continue to volunteer it's a great thing  to do because volunteering helps us as  people but also helps our community and  helps change the world so this week we  just was a thank you on behalf of myself  and Julie and the other partners thank  you so so much we could have done it  without you we thank you for your  volunteering and goodbye  you
 

